meta {
  name: List Referral Panels (Search)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/referral-panels?page=1&limit=20&search=City
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 20
  search: City
  ~clientType: PREPAID
  ~status: ACTIVE
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Paginated list of referral panels in the caller's tenant (newest first).

  ## Filters

  - `search` — case-insensitive match against the panel `name` **OR** the
    user-supplied `panelCode`. Whitespace-only values are ignored. Omit it to list
    all panels.
  - `clientType` — billing relationship. Allowed values: `CASH`, `PREPAID`,
    `POSTPAID`.
  - `status` — active state. Allowed values: `ACTIVE`, `INACTIVE` (mapped to
    `isActive`).

  ## Pagination

  - `page` (default 1) / `limit` (default 20, max 100). Pagination info lands in
    `meta` (`total` / `page` / `limit` / `totalPages`).

  ## Row shape

  Each row is the referral-panel record (scalar columns only), plus `hasActiveOrder`,
  `lastOrderCreatedAt`, `isB2bLoginEnabled` and `labTestList` / `labPanelList` —
  `{ id, name } | null` — the caller's active branch's assigned Lab Test List / Lab
  Panel List, bulk-resolved for the whole page (not a per-row lookup). The raw `branchLabTestListId` / `branchLabPanelListId`
  ids are still only on the single-item response — see *Get Referral Panel*.

  - `hasActiveOrder` — `true` when the panel is used by an order still in an active
    accessioning/technician-stage workflow; the client uses it to disable the Delete
    action (deletion returns **409 `REFERRAL_PANEL_IN_USE`**). Bulk-resolved for the
    whole page.

  - `lastOrderCreatedAt` (ISO date-time | `null`) — when the most recent order using
    this panel was **created** (the order's `createdAt`, UTC; not the user-entered
    order date). Counts every non-deleted order except drafts (`DRAFT`) and
    quotations (`QUOTE`) — appointments and cancelled orders count. `null` when no
    such order exists. Computed live for the whole page (one grouped query).

  - `isB2bLoginEnabled` (boolean) — `true` when the panel has a dedicated B2B login
    (see *Create Referral Panel User*) whose user can sign in: the
    `b2b_referring_panel` profile is active (branch status ACTIVE, not deleted), the
    person is active, and the tenant membership is not `INACTIVE`. `false` when no
    login exists or it has been deactivated. Bulk-resolved for the whole page.
}
